      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T17:17:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it guaranteed that if \"VendorIdSource\" exists in Floss, then \"SdpDiVendorIdSource\" will also exist for all these instances? For example, will a newly paired classic device in Floss only have the Sdp* versions of these and therefore we miss it in the migration from Floss-\u003eBlueZ?",
      "revId": "0bd3f19d43cdbe4407d1ab5322e3c6dbb314d1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0ca5d26_8e3f2483",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/migrate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 682,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T04:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is it guaranteed that if \"VendorIdSource\" exists in Floss, then \"SdpDiVendorIdSource\" will also exist for all these instances?\n\nNo, SdpDi* only exists for classic connection. The Vendor* and Product* version exist for both classic and LE.\n\n\u003e For example, will a newly paired classic device in Floss only have the Sdp* versions of these and therefore we miss it in the migration from Floss-\u003eBlueZ?\n\nNo, newly paired classic device in Floss will have both the Sdp* versions and the Vendor* and Product* versions, therefore we will not miss it (that is, unless the user paired the device using pre-M107 floss and migrate to BlueZ after this CL).\n\nLE connections, on the other hand, only have the Vendor* version. Thus, with this CL, we will not miss it on the Floss-\u003eBlueZ migration, whereas it was missed previously.",
      "parentUuid": "bd908013_4ca0198b",
      "revId": "0bd3f19d43cdbe4407d1ab5322e3c6dbb314d1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c5f4efd_9ee4b42d",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/migrate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 682,
      "author": {
        "id": 1936656
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T00:31:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack. Since the scenario where we will miss this info is quite small and Floss is not fully launched, this is fine with me. Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "d0ca5d26_8e3f2483",
      "revId": "0bd3f19d43cdbe4407d1ab5322e3c6dbb314d1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24625e81_9f5b8070",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/migrate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1074,
      "author": {
        "id": 1936656
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T17:17:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following up on the other questions, does anywhere in the code only use the Sdp* version of these? Is that why we\u0027re keeping both? Your commit mentions they might exist, but do they must exist in the floss conf file?",
      "revId": "0bd3f19d43cdbe4407d1ab5322e3c6dbb314d1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7e0208a_c3979f56",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/migrate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1074,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T04:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only place I see it is \"used\" is [1], which is related to hci metrics logging, a feature that is unimplemented for floss. Therefore, I believe removing it won\u0027t have any negative impact.\n\nHowever, I\u0027m not sure whether they have any other plan of using it in some other way, so I suppose the safest way is to maintain both parameters in floss conf.\n\nWDYT?\n\n[1] https://source.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/aosp/packages/modules/Bluetooth/upstream/system/gd/hci/hci_metrics_logging.cc;l\u003d1099;rcl\u003d3182b13457ab3336097b82544af26597aa8eb114",
      "parentUuid": "24625e81_9f5b8070",
      "revId": "0bd3f19d43cdbe4407d1ab5322e3c6dbb314d1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89dc3778_eff96f56",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/migrate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1074,
      "author": {
        "id": 1936656
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T00:31:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m OK with keeping both since we\u0027re not sure how it will be used later on and it\u0027s not too much to maintain.",
      "parentUuid": "b7e0208a_c3979f56",
